***************************** T A L Y S **************************5046 1451  191
                                                                  5046 1451  192
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   5046 1451  193
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      5046 1451  194
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    5046 1451  195
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     5046 1451  196
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  5046 1451  197
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        5046 1451  198
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    5046 1451  199
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         5046 1451  200
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      5046 1451  201
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    5046 1451  202
stored in this data file:                                         5046 1451  203
                                                                  5046 1451  204
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   5046 1451  205
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     5046 1451  206
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 5046 1451  207
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   5046 1451  208
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                5046 1451  209
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   5046 1451  210
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    5046 1451  211
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        5046 1451  212
- Recoil data                                                     5046 1451  213
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           5046 1451  214
- Total particle energy spectra                                   5046 1451  215
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      5046 1451  216
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        5046 1451  217
- Residual production cross sections                              5046 1451  218
                                                                  5046 1451  219
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            5046 1451  220
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        5046 1451  221
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   5046 1451  222
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                5046 1451  223
                                                                  5046 1451  224
***************** F I L E   I N F O R M A T I O N ****************5046 1451  225
                                                                  5046 1451  226
##### MF1: GENERAL INFORMATION                                    5046 1451  227
                                                                  5046 1451  228
- MT451    : Descriptive data and directory                       5046 1451  229
                                                                  5046 1451  230
This text and the full directory of used MF/MT sections.          5046 1451  231
                                                                  5046 1451  232
##### MF2: RESONANCE PARAMETERS                                   5046 1451  233
                                                                  5046 1451  234
- MT151    : Resonance parameters                                 5046 1451  235
                                                                  5046 1451  236
Details about the origin of the resonance parameters for this     5046 1451  237
nuclide are given above in this description. In general, both a   5046 1451  238
Resolved and an Unresolved Resonance Range are given.             5046 1451  239
                                                                  5046 1451  240
##### MF3: REACTION CROSS SECTIONS                                5046 1451  241
                                                                  5046 1451  242
All the data present in the following MT-sections have been       5046 1451  243
calculated with TALYS, possibly normalized to experimental data.  5046 1451  244
If the maximal cross section in an excitation function over the   5046 1451  245
whole energy range does not exceed 1.e-9 b, the MT-number is not  5046 1451  246
included. Cross sections lower than 1.e-20 b are assumed to have  5046 1451  247
no physical meaning and are set to zero. All MT numbers extend up 5046 1451  248
to the highest incident energy.                                   5046 1451  249
The following reaction channels/MT numbers are generally included:5046 1451  250
                                                                  5046 1451  251
- MT1      : Total cross section                                  5046 1451  252
                                                                  5046 1451  253
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range,    5046 1451  254
or partly reproduced using experimental data.                     5046 1451  255
                                                                  5046 1451  256
- MT2      : Elastic scattering cross section                     5046 1451  257
                                                                  5046 1451  258
Obtained by subtracting the non-elastic cross section from the    5046 1451  259
total cross section.                                              5046 1451  260
                                                                  5046 1451  261
- MT3      : Non-elastic cross section                            5046 1451  262
                                                                  5046 1451  263
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    5046 1451  264
                                                                  5046 1451  265
- MT4      : Total inelastic cross section                        5046 1451  266
                                                                  5046 1451  267
Sum of MT=51-91.                                                  5046 1451  268
                                                                  5046 1451  269
- MT5      : (n,anything) cross section                           5046 1451  270
                                                                  5046 1451  271
MT5 contains the reactions which can not be stored in any other   5046 1451  272
MT-number. The information of MF3/MT5 can be combined with        5046 1451  273
MF6/MT5 to obtain residual production cross sections particle     5046 1451  274
production cross sections and (double-)differential cross         5046 1451  275
sections.                                                         5046 1451  276
                                                                  5046 1451  277
- MT16     : (n,2n) cross section                                 5046 1451  278
- MT17     : (n,3n) cross section                                 5046 1451  279
- MT22     : (n,na) cross section                                 5046 1451  280
- MT28     : (n,np) cross section                                 5046 1451  281
- MT51-90  : (n,n') cross section for 1st-40th excited state      5046 1451  282
- MT91     : (n,n') continuum cross section                       5046 1451  283
- MT102    : (n,gamma) cross section                              5046 1451  284
- MT103    : (n,p) cross section                                  5046 1451  285
- MT104    : (n,d) cross section                                  5046 1451  286
- MT105    : (n,t) cross section                                  5046 1451  287
- MT106    : (n,h) cross section                                  5046 1451  288
- MT107    : (n,a) cross section                                  5046 1451  289
- MT600-610: (n,p) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       5046 1451  290
- MT649    : (n,p) continuum cross section                        5046 1451  291
- MT650-655: (n,d) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        5046 1451  292
- MT699    : (n,d) continuum cross section                        5046 1451  293
- MT700-705: (n,t) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        5046 1451  294
- MT749    : (n,t) continuum cross section                        5046 1451  295
- MT750-755: (n,h) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        5046 1451  296
- MT799    : (n,h) continuum cross section                        5046 1451  297
- MT800-810: (n,a) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       5046 1451  298
- MT849    : (n,a) continuum cross section                        5046 1451  299
                                                                  5046 1451  300
##### MF4: ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY PARTICLES           5046 1451  301
                                                                  5046 1451  302
We use MF4 for the neutron scattering angular distribution for    5046 1451  303
discrete levels.                                                  5046 1451  304
                                                                  5046 1451  305
- MT2      : Elastic angular distribution                         5046 1451  306
                                                                  5046 1451  307
The flag LTT=3 is used to indicate a switch at some high energy,  5046 1451  308
generally 50 MeV, from a Legendre representation to a tabulated   5046 1451  309
representation. For incident energies below this energy, the      5046 1451  310
Legendre coefficients are given on a sufficiently precise energy  5046 1451  311
grid. They are a sum of calculated Legendre coefficients for      5046 1451  312
compound nucleus and shape-elastic scattering. For higher         5046 1451  313
incident energies, relative angular distributions are tabulated   5046 1451  314
on an angular grid.                                               5046 1451  315
                                                                  5046 1451  316
- MT51-70  : (n,n') angular distribution for 1st-20th state       5046 1451  317
- MT600-610: (n,p) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        5046 1451  318
- MT650-655: (n,d) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         5046 1451  319
- MT700-705: (n,t) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         5046 1451  320
- MT750-755: (n,h) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         5046 1451  321
- MT800-810: (n,a) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        5046 1451  322
                                                                  5046 1451  323
##### MF6: PRODUCT ENERGY-ANGLE DISTRIBUTIONS                     5046 1451  324
                                                                  5046 1451  325
In MF6 we store all secondary energy, angle, and energy-angle     5046 1451  326
distributions, as well as all residual and discrete + continuum   5046 1451  327
photon production cross sections for channels other than capture  5046 1451  328
(MT102) and reactions to discrete levels (MT51,etc.).             5046 1451  329
All data are generated with TALYS.                                5046 1451  330
                                                                  5046 1451  331
- MT5      : (n,anything) yields and energy-angle distributions   5046 1451  332
                                                                  5046 1451  333
MT5 contains, in this order,                                      5046 1451  334
For neutrons up to alpha particles and photons:                   5046 1451  335
- the production yields per particle for the whole energy range   5046 1451  336
- the secondary energy-angle distributions per particles which are5046 1451  337
  not represented by explicit MT numbers. On a secondary energy   5046 1451  338
  grid the relative emission spectra are given together with the  5046 1451  339
  parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular              5046 1451  340
  distributions. Inelastic scattering cross sections for discrete 5046 1451  341
  states have been broadened and added to the continuum spectra.  5046 1451  342
For each residual product:                                        5046 1451  343
- the production yields for the whole energy range.               5046 1451  344
- the recoil                                                      5046 1451  345
These distributions can be multiplied with MF3/MT5 to get         5046 1451  346
the production cross sections and (double-)differential cross     5046 1451  347
sections.                                                         5046 1451  348
                                                                  5046 1451  349
- MT16     : (n,2n) energy-angle distr. and photon production     5046 1451  350
                                                                  5046 1451  351
First, for each type of outgoing particle, the (trivial) integer  5046 1451  352
particle yields are given. Next, on a sufficiently dense incident 5046 1451  353
energy grid the secondary energy-angle distributions are          5046 1451  354
specified by means of the relative emission spectra and the       5046 1451  355
parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular distributions. 5046 1451  356
Next, the photon yield is tabulated as a function of incident     5046 1451  357
energy. For each incident energy, the photon production is given  5046 1451  358
for all discrete gamma lines present in the final nucleus. A      5046 1451  359
continuum photon distribution is added to this. We assume         5046 1451  360
isotropy for all produced gamma rays.                             5046 1451  361
                                                                  5046 1451  362
For the following MT-numbers, the same procedure as for MT16 is   5046 1451  363
followed:                                                         5046 1451  364
                                                                  5046 1451  365
- MT17 : (n,3n) energy-angle distr. and photon production         5046 1451  366
- MT22 : (n,na) energy-angle distr. and photon production         5046 1451  367
- MT28 : (n,np) energy-angle distr. and photon production         5046 1451  368
- MT91 : (n,n') continuum energy-angle distr. and phot. prod.     5046 1451  369
- MT649: (n,p) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     5046 1451  370
- MT699: (n,d) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     5046 1451  371
- MT749: (n,t) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     5046 1451  372
- MT809: (n,h) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     5046 1451  373
- MT849: (n,a) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     5046 1451  374
                                                                  5046 1451  375
##### MF8: RADIOACTIVE DECAY DATA                                 5046 1451  376
                                                                  5046 1451  377
For reactions to isomers, MF8 designates where the information    5046 1451  378
for isomeric versus ground state production, or residual          5046 1451  379
production can be found, i.e. for each MT number it points to     5046 1451  380
either MF6, MF9 or MF10.                                          5046 1451  381
                                                                  5046 1451  382
##### MF9: MULTIPLICITIES FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES  5046 1451  383
                                                                  5046 1451  384
MF9 is used for isomer production by non-threshold reactions.     5046 1451  385
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    5046 1451  386
as isomer.                                                        5046 1451  387
                                                                  5046 1451  388
##### MF10: CROSS SECTIONS FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES 5046 1451  389
                                                                  5046 1451  390
MF10 is used for isomer production by threshold reactions.        5046 1451  391
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    5046 1451  392
as isomer.                                                        5046 1451  393
                                                                  5046 1451  394
##### MF12: PHOTON PRODUCTION YIELD DATA                          5046 1451  395
                                                                  5046 1451  396
MF12 is used for the photon production for two types of reactions:5046 1451  397
- Reactions to discrete levels (MT51, etc.) For this transition   5046 1451  398
  probabilities are used (LO=2)                                   5046 1451  399
- Photons from neutron capture (MT102). Here multiplicities are   5046 1451  400
  given                                                           5046 1451  401
                                                                  5046 1451  402
##### MF14: PHOTON ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                          5046 1451  403
                                                                  5046 1451  404
All photon production is considered as isotropic                  5046 1451  405
                                                                  5046 1451  406
##### MF15: PHOTON ENERGY SPECTRA                                 5046 1451  407
                                                                  5046 1451  408
For capture (MT102), the photon energy spectrum is given.         5046 1451  409
                                                                  5046 1451  410
##### MF32: COVARIANCES OF RESONANCE PARAMETERS                   5046 1451  411
                                                                  5046 1451  412
In MF32, we store the covariances of resonance parameters,        5046 1451  413
and more details are given above in this description. In most     5046 1451  414
versions of TENDL, this information is now stored in MF33.        5046 1451  415
                                                                  5046 1451  416
##### MF33: COVARIANCES OF NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS                 5046 1451  417
                                                                  5046 1451  418
In MF33, we store the covariances of most, but not all, reaction  5046 1451  419
channels that are given in MF3. All covariances are generated     5046 1451  420
with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates TALYS runs using    5046 1451  421
a Monte Carlo parameter method.                                   5046 1451  422
For each MT-number, the information consists of:                  5046 1451  423
1. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Ea (variances)                5046 1451  424
2. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Eb (correlations for the      5046 1451  425
   same reaction channel between different energies)              5046 1451  426
3. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Ea (correlations between      5046 1451  427
   different reaction channels for the same energy)               5046 1451  428
4. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Eb (correlations between      5046 1451  429
   different reaction channels for different energies)            5046 1451  430
Classes 1 and 2 are covered by NI-type subsubsections with        5046 1451  431
flag LB=5, followed by a LB=8 section which contains              5046 1451  432
the cross section variances multiplied by 1.e-3. Next, classes 3  5046 1451  433
and 4 are covered by flag LB=6 to account for the different       5046 1451  434
energy grids that two correlating MT-sections may have. Since     5046 1451  435
the total correlation matrix is fully symmetric, we only need to  5046 1451  436
include the correlation elements between different MT-numbers     5046 1451  437
once, and we do that in the subsection with the lowest of the     5046 1451  438
two MT-numbers. We include covariance information for all the     5046 1451  439
total cross sections, the lumped partial cross sections and the   5046 1451  440
individual inelastic cross sections per level (MT51,...). We do   5046 1451  441
not include covariances for MT600 and higher MT-numbers. For the  5046 1451  442
most important channels, we include cross-channel correlations.   5046 1451  443
                                                                  5046 1451  444
##### MF34: COVARIANCES OF ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                  5046 1451  445
                                                                  5046 1451  446
In MF34, we store the covariances of the elastic scattering       5046 1451  447
angular distributions that are given in MF4/MT2. All covariances  5046 1451  448
are generated with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates       5046 1451  449
TALYS runs using a Monte Carlo parameter method. The tables are   5046 1451  450
restricted to MT2 and contain covariances for the first 6         5046 1451  451
Legendre coefficients. Both intra- and inter-correlations of the  5046 1451  452
various Legendre coefficients are given. As in MF33, the LB5      5046 1451  453
representation is used.                                           5046 1451  454
                                                                  5046 1451  455
##### MF40: COVARIANCES OF ISOMER PRODUCTION                      5046 1451  456
                                                                  5046 1451  457
For covariances of ground state and isomeric cross sections, the  5046 1451  458
same procedures as for MF33 are used.                             5046 1451  459
                                                                  5046 1451  460
